# Normalize line endings so a Windows checkout and Linux CI cannot disagree about a
# byte-identical tree. Three real problems came from not having this file:
#
#   * install.sh exited 2 ("manual merge required") on a CRLF checkout without installing
#     anything, so the caller reported the wrong diagnosis.
#   * scripts/build_adapters.py --check compares text-mode strings, which normalizes newlines,
#     so it reported the adapters up to date for a file a rebuild would change.
#   * the same edit produced different bytes depending on who made it, which makes a checksum
#     invariant meaningless.
#
# Shell scripts must be LF or the shebang line breaks. PowerShell is kept CRLF because that is
# what Windows tooling and editors expect for .ps1.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
